{"version": 2, "width": 110, "height": 40, "timestamp": 1788694318, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "linux"}, "title": "token-finops: 04-savings-break-even"}
[0.014686, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ \u001b[0mtoken-finops savings --hardware mac-studio-m4-max-128gb --model qwen3-32b --utilization 0.2\r\n"]
[0.671562, "o", "Local inference: Mac Studio M4 Max, 128 GB + Qwen3 32B (Q4)\r\n  throughput:        25 tok/s  ->  11.11 h per 1M tokens\r\n  energy:            90 W load  ->  1.00 Wh per 1k tok, 1.00 kWh per 1M tok\r\n  tariff:            Germany household (BDEW, Aug 2026) = 0.370 EUR/kWh\r\n  energy cost:       $0.40 / 1M tok\r\n  capex:             $3,999 over 3 y at 20% utilisation = $0.761/h -> $8.45 / 1M tok\r\n  local total:       $8.86 / 1M tok\r\n\r\nCloud comparison (sonnet-class, 15% output tokens): $3.20 / 1M tok  (Claude Sonnet 5)\r\n  -> local is 2.77x the cloud price: CLOUD CHEAPER\r\n  -> break-even utilisation: 60% of 24/7 (14.5 h/day of inference)\r\n  CO2: ~380 g per 1M tok on this tariff\r\n\r\nCaveats: throughput/power figures are editable defaults (see hardware_profiles.json, reviewed 2026-09-04); quality equivalence is an assumption; a sonnet-class local model does not replace Opus/Fable-class work.\r\n"]
[0.681695, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.884172, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ \u001b[0mtoken-finops savings --power solar-de-feed-in --utilization 0.8\r\n"]
[2.54242, "o", "Local inference: Mac Studio M4 Max, 128 GB + Qwen3 32B (Q4)\r\n  throughput:        25 tok/s  ->  11.11 h per 1M tokens\r\n  energy:            90 W load  ->  1.00 Wh per 1k tok, 1.00 kWh per 1M tok\r\n  tariff:            Germany PV self-consumption, opportunity cost = feed-in tariff <=10 kWp (Aug 2026-Jan 2027) = 0.077 EUR/kWh\r\n  energy cost:       $0.08 / 1M tok\r\n  capex:             $3,999 over 3 y at 80% utilisation = $0.190/h -> $2.11 / 1M tok\r\n  local total:       $2.20 / 1M tok\r\n\r\nCloud comparison (sonnet-class, 15% output tokens): $3.20 / 1M tok  (Claude Sonnet 5)\r\n  -> local is 0.69x the cloud price: LOCAL CHEAPER\r\n  -> break-even utilisation: 54% of 24/7 (13.0 h/day of inference)\r\n  CO2: ~40 g per 1M tok on this tariff\r\n\r\nCaveats: throughput/power figures are editable defaults (see hardware_profiles.json, reviewed 2026-09-04); quality equivalence is an assumption; a sonnet-class local model does not replace Opus/Fable-class work.\r\n"]
[2.552709, "o", "\r\n"]
[3.754932, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ \u001b[0mtoken-finops break-even --hardware mac-studio-m4-max-128gb\r\n"]
[4.42983, "o", "Break-even replay: Mac Studio M4 Max, 128 GB running Qwen3 32B (Q4) since 2026-08-24 (14 days)\r\n  replaceable cloud usage (haiku, sonnet-class): 3.3M tokens = $5.07 API-equivalent\r\n"]
[4.430061, "o", "  local alternative:  energy $1.33 + capex $51.13 ($3.65/day straight-line over 3 y) = $52.46\r\n  -> cloud still cheaper by $47.39; at the current pace ($0.36/day) the box never pays off within its lifetime\r\n\r\nAssumptions: only haiku/sonnet-class calls are considered replaceable (edit with --replaceable-tiers); cloud side uses real cache-read/write pricing; the local box has no cache discount but re-processes cached context at full energy cost — that is why cache-heavy agent loops favour the cloud more than raw token counts suggest.\r\n"]
[4.44108, "o", "\r\n"]
